  "slug": "amino-acid-6d41",
  "summary": "Metagenome-derived Cas9 mining, essential-gene interaction maps and kinetic-parameter metabolic models point to scaling functional inference across microbial genomes.",
  "synthesis": "None of the current items uses a sequence language model, so the dominant thread is computational and high-throughput functional characterization of microbial genomes rather than language modeling. NanoPAMDA mines metagenomic data for Cas9 effectors and characterizes their PAMs. A dual-sgRNA CRISPRi platform maps essential-gene genetic interactions in M. smegmatis and M. tuberculosis. kinGEMs pairs CPI-Pred, a deep learning kcat predictor, with uncertainty-aware tuning to build enzyme-constrained metabolic models for 93 organisms, while GEM-CM couples reaction-diffusion models to random-forest surrogates of genome-scale models for P. aeruginosa in gels. gcPathogen 2.0 expands a multi-omics pathogen database. Learned predictors increasingly parameterize mechanistic microbial models, though only kinGEMs uses deep learning explicitly.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-11"
}
